(The favour with which the English public has received the First) Tj T*
(Edition of this translation of Bastiat?s ?Harmonies Économiques?,) Tj T*
(published originally in separate parts, has induced me to have the) Tj T*
(whole reprinted in a cheaper and more accessible form, in the hope of) Tj T*
(giving the work a wider circulation, and rendering it more generally) Tj T*
(useful.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The first ten chapters were all that appeared in the lifetime of the) Tj T*
(gifted author, or that had the benefit of his finishing touch. It) Tj T*
(was Bastiat?s intention, had he lived, to recast the work, and to) Tj T*
(give it a wider and more comprehensive scope; embracing in his design) Tj T*
(not only the principles of Political Economy, but their applications) Tj T*
(to Social Philosophy. Prior to his departure for Italy, on what he) Tj T*
(foresaw might be his last journey, he had communicated to his friends) Tj T*
(MM. de Fontenay and Paillottet a list of the new chapters in the) Tj T*
(order in which they will be found in the subjoined Notice of his) Tj T*
(Life.[1] To the same friends, in his last moments, he entrusted the) Tj T*
(manuscripts intended for the continuation of the work. The duty thus) Tj T*
ET
